# Does a deposition rate in length/time come out right in 3d?
#
# Until this test existed, every rate feature -- units distance, the flux
# source, sticking, mode both, response volume -- was exercised in 2d only.
# The one 3d test in this suite drives the surface with units corner, where
# the direction the surface faces never enters the arithmetic.
#
# 3d is where it matters most.  A corner point field that is binary 0/255
# cannot say which way an oblique surface faces, and the error that follows
# is 1/cos of the angle between the surface normal and the grid.  In 2d that
# tops out at sqrt(2) on a 45 degree plane.  In 3d a facet normal to a cell
# body diagonal gives sqrt(3), so a sphere on a binary field grows
#
#   1.000 along +x, 1.414 along a face diagonal, 1.732 along a body diagonal
#
# which is not just a wrong rate, it is a wrong shape.  read_isurf smooth
# replaces the binary field with a graded one and removes it.
#
# No gas: this is the corner point arithmetic on its own.  Nevery is 5 rather
# than 1 only to keep the test cheap; the rate must not depend on it.

variable            RATE index 0.5
variable            FIELD index sph3d.smooth
variable            SMOOTH index 0
variable            NEVERY index 5

seed                12345
dimension           3
global              gridcut 0.0 comm/sort yes
boundary            r r r

create_box          0 24 0 24 0 24
create_grid         24 24 24
balance_grid        rcb cell

global              nrho 1.0 fnum 1.0
species             air.species N
mixture             air N

variable            rate grid ${RATE}
fix                 ablate ablate all ${NEVERY} 1.0 v_rate mode deposit &
                    units distance

global              surfs implicit
read_isurf          all 24 24 24 ${FIELD} 127.5 ablate push no smooth ${SMOOTH}

surf_collide        1 diffuse 300.0 1.0
surf_modify         all collide 1
timestep            0.001

dump                G grid all 2000 tmp.rate3d.grid id xlo ylo zlo f_ablate[1]
dump_modify         G pad 0

stats               2000
stats_style         step f_ablate f_ablate[21]
run                 2000
